 "conclusions_retained": [
  "On the primary greedy reading the calibrated critic init preserved the R68 task outcome exactly in all three seeds: 183 on-time targets over 32 scenes, identical on-time target ID sets, task delta 0, CI [0,0], zero targets lost or gained.",
  "On the primary greedy reading the cost change is exactly zero in all three seeds: 4066.5 B per scene, delta 0.0, CI [0,0], zero scenes cheaper, zero scenes dearer, zero changed first-report events.",
  "The early key target scene 1700027 / piloc-e1-target-5 is preserved in all three seeds under both the calibrated init and the trained model: 6/6 on-time, 7500 B, first report at step 134 in the early region.",
  "The calibrated init reproduces the R68 initial policy bit-for-bit on the focal scene: NEW_INIT minus R68_INIT_ALPHA is task 0 and cost 0 with identical target ID sets in all three seeds.",
  "Every observed first-report difference is confined to the late region; the early region is bit-identical in every cell because trunk and early_head are frozen by the inherited R66/R68 intervention."
 ],
 "conclusions_deferred": [
  "No cost reduction: sampled cost direction is -155.8 / +331.1 / -642.2 B per scene across seeds 11/22/33, so the cross-seed direction is not consistent, and seed 22 sampled is significantly MORE expensive (CI [78.4, 662.6] excludes 0).",
  "Seed 33 sampled loses one on-time target versus R68 (scene 1800019 / piloc-e1-target-0) and both seed 11 and seed 33 sampled lose 3 on-time targets versus the IMMEDIATE rule.",
  "The greedy bit-identity is partly structural (frozen early path plus a two-way head), not evidence that critic calibration is behaviourally neutral in general.",
  "ROUND71 added offline teacher exposure that R68 did not have: 70,693 real trunk-input rows over 78 calls. This is NOT a same-training-budget race against R68 and must not be read as one.",
  "Eval block 1800000..1800031 is an already-used development block, not an unseen confirmation set; n=32 scenes per cell, one random realisation per cell, three seeds not pooled, and a CI containing 0 is not equivalence.",
  "These results support only the whole critic-initialisation-calibration structure on this development block. They do not prove the uncalibrated critic init was the only root cause and they do not support generalisation, formal non-inferiority or deployment."
 ],
